p=O/'physics-development.html';h=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');section='''<section id="curved-added-hidden-state"><h2>Rechecking hidden initial canopy state</h2><p>The latest model was given six fitted initial canopy attitude/rate adjustments using each complete three-second target trajectory, with aerodynamic and inertia coefficients frozen. This uses future observations and is not predictive validation. It is a bounded local fit, not a mathematical upper bound on achievable model accuracy.</p><img src="iteration-curved-added-hidden-state.png" alt="Bank and heading errors before and after fitting hidden initial canopy states to future observations" style="max-width:100%"><p>HR 450 heading error falls from 110.9° to 44.5°, and TL 402 falls from 36.6° to 2.7°. Some bank errors worsen because the objective balances attitude, velocity, and initial force consistency. Two cases reach the allowed angular-rate adjustment bounds. These are not measured canopy rates.</p><p>Initial-state uncertainty materially affects heading prediction, but this local diagnostic still cannot reproduce the hardest Hood River turns adequately. A past-only state estimator should be evaluated on actual forecasts; fitting future initial states cannot be counted as a successful simulator.</p></section>'''
if 'id="curved-added-hidden-state"' not in h:h=h.replace('</body>',section+'\n</body>');p.write_text(h,encoding='utf-8')
